From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 08:02:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01753/11362] [outer-loop] fix the over-claimed DiffusionGemma
 gate: MET -> STILL-PENDING (operator-directed)

The .387 capstone (exp4183) flipped diffusiongemma_gate_status to MET on exp4177
(+0.18 on code/HumanEval). That is the TRIVIAL/circular case: there the verifier IS
the executable oracle (run the unit tests), so it does not show a non-trivial/energy/
learned verifier adds value. On the domain that matters (ARC, ~13pp real headroom) the
verifier TIES vote (exp4178 GAP-3 BOUNDED, delta 0); the .388 C1 DiffusionGemma run
(exp4189) blocked on absent weights anyway. Corrected to STILL-PENDING in 3 places:
 - the canonical gate definition (spec): tightened to require a NON-TRIVIAL verifier
   beating a matched control on a headroom-present, oracle-DISTINCT domain (ARC); status
   marked STILL-PENDING.
 - exp4183 capstone artifact: status->STILL-PENDING + corrigendum (original preserved).
 - .388 roadmap milestone_overview prose.
Downstream artifacts (exp4174 archive, exp4189 C1) already recorded honest status. The
.388 capstone reads those, so it won't re-assert MET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
